{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/619","id":5054508733,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-xXos8AAAABLUWuvQ","html_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/619","diff_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/619.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/619.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/619","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/619/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/619/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/619/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/statuses/99b63e767789dc7f1b363bd888b3e821b234a11d","number":619,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ds4: a sampler CUDA error is checked and ends the request (no token -1 to the client); logits() copies on d.st","user":{"login":"SeriousRising","id":69419008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDE5MDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69419008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising","html_url":"https://github.com/SeriousRising","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #616.\n\n**What.**\n\n- `src/ds4/ds4_model.cu`: `tok_back(d)` does the sampled token's copy + sync with both return codes checked. On a CUDA error it prints `ds4 sample: <error>` and returns -1. `sample_row`, `sample` and `sample_multi` use it.\n- `src/ds4/ds4_main.cpp`: one check where a token is emitted, so every sampler and caller is covered. Serve (`T %d`) and `--parallel` (`T <rid> %d`) print `ds4: the sample failed` and finish the request with `cancel` instead of sending token -1; the CLI exits 1 before the token goes into its output.\n- `logits()`: `cudaMemcpyAsync` on `d.st` + `cudaStreamSynchronize`, both checked, instead of a `cudaMemcpy` on the legacy stream (not ordered after the non-blocking `d.st`).\n\n**Output: unchanged** (error paths and copy ordering only; no sync is added, each sampler already synchronised `d.st`). 2x CMP 170HX 64 GB (sm_80, CUDA 12.8; PCIe Gen2 x16 + Gen2 x4), DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 GSQ-RCO IQ2_XXS, `--tp 1 --gpus 0,1 --dspark on --cpu-threads 14 --suffix-draft 0`: 2000 fixed prompt ids + 256 greedy tokens give the same ids and the same DSpark rounds / offered / accepted / per-position counts as v1.1.35. No speed change expected and none measured beyond that run.\n\n**Not tested:** the error path itself (it needs an injected CUDA fault).\n\n**Checks** (as `.github/workflows/tests.yml`): `tools/check_hip_compat.py` OK; server tests 463 OK (12 skipped); installer and tools tests 584 OK (31 skipped) - the same counts as v1.1.35.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T17:05:19Z","updated_at":"2026-10-28T21:11:03Z","closed_at":"2026-10-28T21:11:03Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a8474ed44a05e20c293f15f0eb9ac3e05d787233","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"SeriousRising:ds4-sample-error-checks","ref":"ds4-sample-error-checks","repo":{"id